.TH FIN 1 "2026" "fin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fin \- terminal UI client for Jellyfin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fin
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfin\fR is a terminal UI application for browsing and playing media
from a Jellyfin media server.
It supports library browsing, full-text search, item details with optional
cover art (Kitty graphics protocol), and media playback via mpv.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " DIR"
Use
.I DIR
as the configuration directory instead of the XDG default.
Both the config file and credentials file are read from this directory.
.TP
.B \-\-version ", " \-v
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fin/config.toml
TOML configuration file.
.RS
.TP
.B [player] command
Media player command.
Default:
.BR mpv .
.TP
.B [player] extra_args
Additional arguments passed to the player.
.TP
.B [server] url
Jellyfin server URL.
Pre-filled after first login.
.RE
.TP
.I ~/.config/fin/credentials
AES\-GCM encrypted credentials file, keyed by machine ID.
Delete this file to log out.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the base directory for configuration files.
When set, the config directory is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fin
instead of
.IR ~/.config/fin .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
